    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="blog-section" id="mistake">
    <h2>Common Building Measurement Mistakes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Adding length and width instead of multiplying them.</li>
      <li>Counting the same extension twice.</li>
      <li>Including a garage when the project requires living area only.</li>
      <li>Forgetting a second or third floor.</li>
      <li>Mixing interior and exterior measurements.</li>
      <li>Using feet-and-inches values incorrectly without converting.</li>
      <li>Measuring only the largest rectangle and ignoring smaller sections.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Keep all measurements in a written table — this makes the calculation easy to verify and update if you find an error.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="blog-section" id="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <% const _faqs = [["How do you calculate the square footage of a building?", "Multiply length × width for each rectangular section, then add the areas of all sections and floors together."], ["Does building square footage include all floors?", "Total building square footage typically includes all floors, but the exact definition depends on the purpose and measurement standard. Confirm with your local authority or appraiser."], ["Do I include the garage?", "Include the garage only if the calculation requires total building area. Exclude it when calculating finished living space or heated floor area."], ["How do you calculate square footage of an L-shaped building?", "Divide the L-shape into two rectangles. Calculate the area of each rectangle, then add the results together."], ["What is the difference between footprint and total square footage?", "The footprint is the ground-level area covered by the building. Total square footage includes all floors stacked on top of that footprint."]]; _faqs.forEach(function(f) { %>
